Title: Is this all on Runware?
Credit: Script. 60 seconds. Every line every character says.
Source: /home/felipe-lopez/Desktop/Runware Test/Creative Task Runware/Script/Script (Scene 1 to 3)/Script Final/SCRIPT.md
Draft date: 2026-11-19

INT. THE STOREROOM. NIGHT. #sc-1#

A vaulted storeroom: crates, barrels, sacks. The lantern hangs from the dwarf's axe; one torch burns beside a stone staircase that climbs along the right wall into a dark doorway. Seven travellers rest in a loose circle. Food is being divided on a crate.

= 1A, 0 to 5 s

VESSA
(cutting bread on a crate, warm, teasing)
That's your half, Borrin. The small one.

BORRIN
(slurred, cheerful, flask in hand)
I had the smaller half last time, lads. I measured.

DAX
(bouncing by the foot of the stairs, bright)
He measured with his mouth.

VEL
(by the crates, not looking up, flat)
Two days of food. Keep your voices down.

= 1B, 5 to 9 s

OSWIN
(leaning on his staff, eyes shut, quietly to himself)
...and the waters shall know their own...

BORRIN
(sniffing toward the barrels, half joking)
Smells like a pond in here. A dead pond.

SYLWEN
(eyes closed, back to the right wall, even)
The barrel moved.

The black water in the open barrel ripples. From the dark doorway above the stairs, a wet chirping, very faint, then not faint.

= 1C, 9 to 15 s

MORDECAI
(at the back of the circle, pleased, raising one hand; green flame flares from his palm and lights the stairs)
Company.

Dozens of gold eyes open in the dark doorway above the stairs. The first frogs pour down the steps into the light. Behind the party the barrel lids rock and frogs burst out of the barrels too.

VEL
(on her feet, rapier out, two words)
Lantern up. Line.

VESSA
(roaring, delighted, kissing the broken blade, shield up)
FINALLY.

DAX
(leaping onto the stairs)
One!

OSWIN
(left hand already up, horrified)
Oh no. Oh no, no, those are...

INT. THE CORRIDOR. CONTINUOUS. #sc-2#

A long flooded passage that begins at the top of the storeroom's stairs. The party comes out of the stair doorway and advances toward the far archway in a loose fighting line, lantern in front, green fire at the back. Frogs and toads on the floor, the bench, the walls, the chains.

= 2A, 15 to 20 s

MORDECAI
(from the top of the stairs, one arm flung out; a ring of green fire rolls down the corridor; counting with relish)
Eleven.

VEL
(lunging, flat)
Nine.

MORDECAI
(delighted)
Assists are not kills, Captain.

DAX
(leaping from the top of the stairs over the barrels onto a toad)
Seven!

VESSA
(as he skids and lands on his back)
Six and a half.

= 2B, 20 to 24 s

OSWIN
(left hand high; a wave rolls down the passage and the frogs sit in it, shining)
They're AMPHIBIANS. They should... I don't understand...

SYLWEN
(bandaging her own hand, walking, even)
That one was yours, Oswin.

BORRIN
(head-butting a toad with his helmet, then raising the flask to it)
To you, big lad.

A toad slams Vessa flat on her back among the frogs. She laughs, gets up.

= 2C, 24 to 30 s

The frogs thin. The last of them run PAST the party toward the way they came. Vel stops. The others stop behind her.

VEL
(quiet, cold)
They're not attacking.

VEL
(looking at the archway and the grey light)
They're running.

BORRIN
(quiet for once)
Told you. Pond.

MORDECAI
(low, happy)
Oh, good.

Vel walks to the archway and steps through it into the grey light.

EXT. THE ROOFLESS HALL OF THE FALLEN CASTLE. NIGHT. #sc-3#

The great hall of the ruin, roofless, under a vast starry sky. A stone bench with the last frogs on it; beyond it a mound of rubble sunk in black bubbling mud, something huge coiled around it under the muck. The party fans out from the archway.

= 3A, 30 to 35 s

VEL
(one hand up, stopping everyone, watching the mud)
Nobody on the mud.

DAX
(two bounces on his toes, grinning)
Define "on".

The mud bulges. A ripple runs toward the lantern.

SYLWEN
(even)
Borrin. Step back.

= 3B, 35 to 40 s

The coil around the mound heaves; the worm rears up out of the mud in a column of muck and SCREAMS. The frogs scatter from the bench toward it.

OSWIN
(praying fast, water gathering at his hand)
Lord of the deep water, Lord of the deep water, Lord of the...

MORDECAI
(over the scream, arms spreading wide, thrilled)
Now THAT is worth getting up for.

VEL
(throwing a pot; green hiss)
Flanks! Vessa, the collar!

= 3C, 40 to 45 s

VESSA
(hacking at the worm's collar as it rears, laughing through her teeth)
It's SOFT. Why is it SOFT.

The coil sweeps the ground: Vessa goes down flat on her back behind her shield, and the coil closes round Sylwen, pinning her to the waist, her arms free. Oswin's wave hits its flank.

OSWIN
(astonished at himself)
It worked. It WORKED.

SYLWEN
(from inside the coil, reaching down to Vessa's bleeding arm, green light in her palms, dry)
Hold still. Yes, it's soft. Hold still.

= 3D, 45 to 51 s

The sky opens: rain in sheets, backlit green. Dax runs up the fallen blocks at the back of the hall.

DAX
(launching, both hands on the Halfblade)
EIGHT!

He lands on the worm's head and drives the half blade in to the crossguard. The worm screams and rears; he slips on the slick skin and slides down its side into the mud. The coil loosens.

VESSA
(scrambling up, raw)
DAX!

VEL
(into the mud, hauling Sylwen out of the coil by both arms, through her teeth, to Dax)
I said. Nobody. On the mud.

= 3E, 51 to 56 s

The worm rears to its full height and SCREAMS, mouth wide open. Mordecai stands on the highest block, tabard streaming, both arms raised wide, green flame blazing in both hands.

MORDECAI
(grandly, to Vel, as the mouth opens)
Watch closely, Captain. This one is mine.

A beam of green soul-flame from his hands down the worm's throat. Lightning. The body spasms and falls across the mound.

VEL
(setting Sylwen down beside Dax, flat, not looking at Mordecai)
Assist.

MORDECAI
(outraged, delighted)
It is NOT an assist.

= 3F, 56 to 60 s

SMASH CUT. Silence but the rain. The seven of them, soaked and filthy, standing and sitting in the mud before the dead worm, all looking up at the enormous starry sky through the roofless walls. The lantern on the axe is a faint ember. Long beat.

BORRIN
(quiet, slurred, utterly sincere, raising the flask to the stars)
...is this all on Runware?

Vel looks at him. Cut to black.

TITLE CARD (white serif on black, 2 s):

> Is this all on Runware? <
